cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Faspy: quantification of vascular bundles in FASGA-stained palm
  leaflet sections
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
version: 1.0.0

# TODO before publication: complete every field marked FIXME.
authors:
  - given-names: Paul
    family-names: Cathelineau
    affiliation: Institut de Recherche pour le Developpement (IRD)
    email: paul.cathelineau@ird.fr
    orcid: FIXME          # https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000

repository-code: https://github.com/paulcathelineau/Faspy
license: MIT

abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline that measures vascular bundle number, bundle area and
  lumen area on transverse sections of FASGA-stained palm leaflets. Bundles are
  segmented as instances with a fine-tuned Cellpose-SAM model; the leaflet
  footprint is segmented with a U-Net and provides the denominator of every
  ratio. Five-fold cross-validation over 151 annotated sections gives an object
  F1 of 0.934 and a counting error of 6.9 per cent.

keywords:
  - plant anatomy
  - quantitative histology
  - image segmentation
  - FASGA staining
  - Cellpose

